# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# StageZero Environment Configuration
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Copy this file to .env and update values for your environment
# DO NOT commit .env to source control
#
# Nothing in here is required. The compose files pass this file into the
# container; `dotnet run` and the VS Code launch read it from the repo root.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# APPLICATION
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Log level: Verbose, Debug, Information, Warning, Error. Default: Debug in Development,
# Information otherwise.
# STAGEZERO_LOG_LEVEL=Information

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DATABASE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SQLite in the data directory unless these say PostgreSQL. A misspelt provider, or
# postgres without a connection string, stops startup. Move an existing SQLite install
# with `copy-to-postgres` (README, Database).
# STAGEZERO_DB_PROVIDER=postgres
# STAGEZERO_DB_CONNECTION=Host=db;Database=stagezero;Username=stagezero;Password=change-me
#
# For docker-compose.postgres.yml, which runs PostgreSQL beside the app and builds the
# connection string itself. No ';' in it.
# POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
#
# For docker-compose.provision.yml, which lets Settings → Database create StageZero's own
# PostgreSQL container by mounting the Docker socket (read that file's header: the socket is
# root on the host). The socket belongs to the engine's docker group; give the container
# that group id. Linux: the command below. VM engines (BoxCar, Colima, OrbStack): "Look for
# PostgreSQL" on the Settings page names the number when it is wrong. Docker Desktop
# usually needs nothing (0 is the default).
# DOCKER_GID=$(stat -c %g /var/run/docker.sock)

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CONTAINER DATA (docker-compose.yml)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Host directory mounted at /app-data in the release container: the database, logs
# and the data-protection keys that decrypt the stored Cloudflare tokens. Default
# ./.volumes/stagezero-data; docker-run.sh uses the platform's app-data directory.
# The debug container keeps its own, STAGEZERO_DEBUG_DATA_DIR, default
# ./.volumes/stagezero-debug.
# STAGEZERO_DATA_DIR=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# EMAIL: NONE
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# StageZero does not send email. A "forgot password" code is written to the
# application log (`docker logs stagezero` in Docker) as a banner headed
# STAGEZERO PASSWORD RESET CODE. Nothing to configure.

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CODELIFTER.NET (OPTIONAL)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# The first-run page registers the admin email with codelifter.net (a box,
# ticked by default; it subscribes nobody and sends nothing). Settings offers the
# CodeLifter newsletter and StageZero updates, each with its own confirmation
# email. To switch all of it off (a fork, an air-gapped install), set the URL
# to blank:
# CodeLifter__SubscriptionsUrl=

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CLOUDFLARE TUNNEL (OPTIONAL — DOCKER SIDECAR ONLY)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Only needed if you run the cloudflared connector as a container instead of a
# host service. Get the token from StageZero's Tunnel Setup page, then start the
# release stack with:
#   docker compose --profile tunnel up -d
#
# Running cloudflared as a host service (macOS launchd / Windows service /
# systemd) is the recommended setup — the connector then survives the app stack
# going down. See ..Documentation/CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_SETUP.md.
#
# Treat this like a password: it grants the ability to serve traffic on your
# tunnel's hostnames.
# TUNNEL_TOKEN=
